.TH CADROP 1 "August 23, 2026" "VirtualSquare Labs"
.SH NAME
cadrop \- execute a command after dropping ambient capabilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cadrop
[
.I capability-list | all | -
[
.I command
[
.I args ...
]
]
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cadrop
removes the selected ambient and inheritable capabilities, then executes the
command. If the command is omitted it uses
.BR $SHELL .
.PP
Omitting the capability argument, using
.BR all ,
or using
.B -
drops every ambient capability. These are the only all-capability forms; an empty
string is invalid. A specific capability list uses the strict name/mask grammar
documented in
.BR cado (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cado (1),
.BR caprint (1),
.BR capabilities (7)
